NEARS-1776 QA — the FIXED build still red-screens on a cold store deep-link
Device emulator-5554, HEAD build c092e66c, installed APK md5 0d974fd609872637d0ed476a435a6f52
(md5 re-verified identical before AND after the 30-attempt run).

RESULT: 29 of 30 attempts = full-screen 'Null check operator used on a null value'
        (RED_FRACTION 0.993). 1 attempt unclassified (app still on splash at t+22s).
        BASE (unfixed, 5ab0de66) over the identical harness: 29/30.

WHY THE FIX DOES NOT COVER IT — the throw happens BEFORE StoreScreen exists:
  * In 58/58 red attempts across both builds, /api/v1/stores/details NEVER fired,
    i.e. StoreScreen.initState never ran, i.e. its Scaffold.floatingActionButton
    Visibility chain (the site NEARS-1776 guards) was never evaluated.
  * In the ONE attempt that rendered the store screen, stores/details fired 4x
    and it is also the ONLY attempt logging configNull=false.
  * Perfect correlation: 29/29 red attempts log 'route: checkModuleId configNull=true';
    the single clean attempt logs configNull=false.

ACTUAL THROW SITE — UserApp/lib/helper/route_helper.dart, RouteHelper.getRoute():
  static Widget getRoute(
    Widget navigateTo, {
    AccessLocationScreen? locationScreen,
    bool byPuss = false,
  }) {
    double? minimumVersion = 0;
    if (GetPlatform.isAndroid) {
      minimumVersion =
          Get.find<SplashController>().configModel!.appMinimumVersionAndroid;
    } else if (GetPlatform.isIOS) {
      minimumVersion =
          Get.find<SplashController>().configModel!.appMinimumVersionIos;
    }
    return (AppConstants.appVersion < minimumVersion!)
        ? const UpdateScreen(isUpdate: true)
        : Get.find<SplashController>().configModel!.maintenanceMode!
        ? const UpdateScreen(isUpdate: false)
        : (AddressHelper.getUserAddressFromSharedPref() == null && !byPuss)

_storePage() is 'getRoute(_waitForModule(...))'. Dart evaluates the argument first —
which is why 'route: waiting for module=' and the checkModuleId lines DO appear —
then getRoute's body runs and null-asserts configModel at line 1474 while config is
still in flight. getRoute( is called 37x in route_helper.dart, so every one of those
routes has the same exposure on a cold deep-link / notification tap.

